{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2349-recipes-for-gaming-groups","id":2349,"title":"Recipes for Gaming groups.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-03T21:12:34-08:00","id":2349,"title":"Recipes for Gaming groups.","content":"With the upcoming release of the Werewolf cookbook I decided to post a recipe or two that I make for my gaming group. The first one is for <b>Chicken Pot Pie Pennsylvania Dutch Style</b><br /> Ingredients:<br /> 1 Chicken whole preferably a stewing chicken<br /> Celery about 4-6 stalks<br /> 1 medium onion<br /> 12 carrots<br /> 2 bags of noodles either ribbon or square <br /> <br /> Dice the celery and onion mix them together place the chicken, celery and onions in a large pot(3 quarts or larger) fill about half way with water and bring to a boil. Turn the heat to low once it boils <br /> let the chicken simmer until the chicken is falling off the bone.(I use a pot with a colander/strainer) remove the chicken from the broth and pull the meat off of the bones separating out the skin, fat and gristle as well. Return the meat and the onions and celery to the stock. add the carrots and bring the mixture back to a boil. Once it is boiling add the noodles and cook until soft.<br /> <br /> Feeds approx. 8-12 people depending on the size of the chicken and appetites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:50:01-08:00","id":2414,"title":"","content":"One thing I like to do is to get a tortilla. Then I chop up some onions and mix it up with like tuna and herbs and chillis and a little lime juice and coriander and then I dump a little in the tortilla and fold it up. Then I put that thing in the oven for like ten minutes or whatever and it's pretty tasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T13:30:28-08:00","id":2864,"title":"","content":"I find a recipe with good reviews and enough ingredients to satisfy the number of people in the group (and then some) <a href=\"http://crockpot365.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">at this slow cooker blog</a>. I can make sure that everybody's dietary restrictions are honored that way, keep things cheap, and make sure there's enough food to last us. I toss everything in, set it to cook, and go about prepping the game. Sometimes we have to add side dishes, but even those can be fast and cheap, like potatoes. Everybody eats, it's delicious, and requires minimal fuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:28:56-08:00","id":2908,"title":"","content":"A hallowed recipe from the depths of my hard drive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> take a bigass bag of oreos, put them in a ziploc, and crush them. crush them real good.<br /> take a mixer and fluff up some softened cream cheese<br /> once fluffy, add the oreos and mix them up some more.<br /> let that chill in a freezer for a bit, then take it and roll the mix into little balls<br /> melt up some almond bark and semisweet morsels and dip the oreo balls in the melted chocolate<br /> then let those chill a bit. keep them in a freezer.<br /> what you get is a hellishly decadent oreo-cheesecake ball covered in chocolate<br /> you can tool around with this of course, however you like<br /> crushed reeses pieces also work hella awesome </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T17:42:55-08:00","id":3052,"title":"","content":"Cheap-ass beef tips<br /> <br /> 1 package of stew meat (I usually get the large package)<br /> 1 envelope of onion mushroom soup mix<br /> 1/2 stick of butter (the real stuff)<br /> <br /> Spray sides and bottom of crock pot, toss in butter, followed by stew meat. Sprinkle the onion mushroom soup mix all over the meat. Set crock pot to 6 hours on high. Start stirring at 2 hours, at 2 hour intervals. If the meat is tender by 4 hours, boil up egg noodles by directions on package. When al-dente, drain and put noodles in the crock pot, mixing everything together. If wanted, stir in sour cream (amount usually as much as you want). Turn crock pot to warm or off, depending on the age of your crock pot and the size (I have a 5 quart/10 hour with warm option machine).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:48:47-08:00","id":20568,"title":"","content":"*note to self. My game group will need a crock pot* Thanks guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:11:55-08:00","id":21744,"title":"","content":"Oh, for the days I had both the time and the space to host games at my place. Last time I was able to do that, I was a pretty shitty cook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1358-polisurgist","name":"Polisurgist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}